CORE gcc-only
main.c

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A reduced-alignment typedef used as a struct member keeps its alignment (as
GCC/Clang/icx do), while a reducing alignment attribute on the member
declarator is ignored. The two are distinguished by the
C_alignment_increase_only provenance flag.
